 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "hotpoint SA2 oven not heatin on fan, grill ok. wat does SA2 mean??"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "SA2 is likely a model series code for your Hotpoint cooker rather than an error message. Since the grill works but the fan oven doesn't heat, the most common cause is a failed fan heating element (the ring-shaped heater at the back). However, it could also be the selector switch or thermostat. To narrow this down: when you turn on the fan oven function, does the fan inside actually spin and blow air? Please check this with the oven door closed for safety."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "no the fan isnt spinning, just a low hum from the back. it was noisy for a few weeks b4 that, grinding/squeal at startup"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Failed fan motor]\nThe hum is the motor trying to turn but being physically blocked by internal friction. Because this involves opening the oven cavity and disconnecting electrical components, you need a qualified engineer or electrician to replace the fan motor safely. Please switch off the power at the mains before calling them."
  }
 ],
